# What never enters a build context (WP-24).
#
# This file is the first line of defence and is deliberately not the only one:
# `pgx-deploy build` inspects the built image's filesystem afterwards and fails
# on anything matching FORBIDDEN_IMAGE_PREFIXES in
# pgx/deployment/runtime_assets.py. An ignore file states an intention; the
# post-build check measures the result, and only the second one would catch a
# COPY that named a path this file forgot.
#
# The ordering below is by *why*, not alphabetical, because the reasons are the
# reviewable part.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and key material. Nothing here is ever in an image layer, including
# an intermediate one - a deleted file in an earlier layer is still in the
# image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
deploy/secrets/
deploy/tls/
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Restricted and scientific-input data. The image gets a named allowlist of
# artifacts the serving path reads; everything else under data/ is a build
# input, a baseline, or - in the case of holdout - something that must never
# be in a container at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/
data/canonical/
data/evidence/
data/legacy-baseline/
data/migration/
data/curation/
data/holdout/
data/reports/
data/coverage/
data/rulesets/
data/assessments/
data/expert-review/
data/_to_delete/
_to_delete/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frozen legacy artifacts. They are WP-01 evidence and are never runtime code;
# packaging them would put a legacy entry point inside the deployment image,
# which the WP-24 brief forbids and which architecture.md section 15 step 10
# already rules out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clinpgx_probe.py
clinpgx_probe_v2.py
clean_mvp_seed_dataset.py
risk_engine.py
gemini_report_generator.py
candidate_onboarding.py
alternative_ranker.py
clinpgx_mvp_seed/
clinpgx_outputs/
clinpgx_outputs_v2/
final_report/
candidate_alternatives.csv
drug_graph_edges.csv
MVP_1_TEKNIK_DURUM_RAPORU.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development environments, caches and generated output. Copying a .venv is
# how an image ends up with a host's interpreter path baked into a shebang.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv-linux/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.tmp/
.cache/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests and their fixtures. Not because they are secret, but because an image
# containing a test suite contains its fixtures - including the WP-20 unsafe
# controls, which are deliberately dangerous code that exists to be detected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/
scripts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and compose files. Read by people, not by the runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
README.md.bak
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
